# ── lanthanides.io — example environment ─────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to `.env` for local development if you want the contributions inbox.
# `.env` is gitignored; never commit real credentials (CLAUDE.md hard rule #3).
#
# DATABASE_URL is the ONLY variable the app reads, and it is optional. It points
# at the Neon Postgres holding the single contributions-inbox table
# (db/schema.sql; create it once with `npm run db:init`). The inbox stores
# community price contributions and nothing else.
#
# Unset, the site still works fully: /contribute marks the queue unavailable
# and POST /api/contributions returns 503. The build never reads the database.
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@ep-example-pooler.region.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require"
